Environment

Environment: Production (public demo site)
URL: https://www.saucedemo.com/checkout-step-two.html
Build / Version: index-DnLqFcJI.js
Device: Desktop
OS: Windows 11
Browser: Chrome
User role / Test account: standard_user

Description
Checkout has two steps: “Your Information”, where First Name, Last Name and Zip/Postal Code are required, and “Overview”. The Overview page doesn’t check that step one was completed. A user can open /checkout-step-two.html directly and click “Finish”, and the order goes through with no first name, last name or postal code. In the same way, /checkout-complete.html can be opened directly and shows “Thank you for your order!” even though no order was placed.

Preconditions
User is logged in as standard_user.
At least one product is in the cart.

Steps to Reproduce
Log in as standard_user and add any product to the cart.
Don’t click “Checkout”. Open https://www.saucedemo.com/checkout-step-two.html directly.
Click “Finish”.
Click “Generate PDF order” and open the PDF.
Separately, open https://www.saucedemo.com/checkout-complete.html directly.

Test Data
Product: Sauce Labs Backpack

Actual Result
The Overview page opens without the “Your Information” step.
“Finish” places the order and shows “Thank you for your order!”.
The PDF receipt has no “Ship To” section, because no name or postal code was entered [To confirm].
Opening /checkout-complete.html directly shows “Thank you for your order!” with no order.

Expected Result
Opening /checkout-step-two.html before finishing step one sends the user back to “Checkout: Your Information”.
An order can only be finished when First Name, Last Name and Zip/Postal Code are filled in.
Opening /checkout-complete.html without a finished order sends the user to the Products page.

Reproducibility
Always (worked out from the code) [To confirm in the browser]

Impact
Orders can be created without shipping details.
The “Thank you” page can appear without an order, which is confusing.
Workaround: None.

Attachments
https://jam.dev/c/67f6574e-c20e-41a5-946f-1d6d1ada5980

Suggested Fix (optional)
On the Overview page, check that the checkout details exist. If they don’t, send the user back to step one.
On the Complete page, show the thank-you message only right after an order is placed.

Acceptance Criteria
Given the user hasn’t completed “Your Information”, when they open /checkout-step-two.html, then they’re sent to /checkout-step-one.html.
Given no order was just placed, when the user opens /checkout-complete.html, then they’re sent to the Products page.
Given the normal flow, when the user fills in step one and clicks “Finish”, then the order completes as before and the PDF shows the Ship To details.
